From: "omharde@4" <you@example.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 11:12:13 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 04/12] fix(auth): sign Discord OAuth state and require auth to
 initiate account linking
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Discord's OAuth `state` was attacker-controllable base64 JSON. An attacker
could run their own Discord authorize flow with state = { action: 'link',
userId: '<victim>' }, then the callback would link the ATTACKER's Discord
account to the VICTIM's GamerHub account — giving the attacker a permanent
login to the victim's account (account takeover, critical).

- oauth.ts: signOAuthState/verifyOAuthState - HMAC-SHA256 signed state with
  nonce, timestamp and 10-minute expiry; constant-time comparison; fails closed.
- discordRedirect: login only; state is now signed. The old
  ?action=link&userId= flow is removed (it was the vulnerable path).
- NEW authenticated POST /auth/discord/link: binds the link to req.user, signs
  a state containing the current user's id, and returns the Discord authorize
  URL. The callback only trusts signed states.
- discordCallback: uses config.apiUrl for redirect_uri (no Host header) and
  verifies state before honoring action/userId.
- web settings page now starts Discord linking via the authenticated endpoint.

Tests: oauth.test.ts - state round-trip, wrong-secret rejection, tampered
payload rejection, expiry, malformed input.

Run: cd server && npx jest src/utils/oauth.test.ts

